{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CLOSE EVIDENCE: Gerrit change 2141 MERGED to main as aa0668b0ee3 (LLM-Review +1 from the rebar review bot, Verified +1 from CI run 32611006643, zero unresolved comments; submitted 2026-08-23 02:27 UTC). All ACs verified: (1) timeout_func_only removed from [tool.pytest.ini_options] — config arm test_the_configured_budget_is_the_measured_one asserts the key's ABSENCE and fails on reappearance; (2) hanging SETUP and TEARDOWN are bounded and named — out-of-process arms test_a_hanging_fixture_setup_is_bounded_by_the_ini and test_a_hanging_teardown_is_bounded_by_the_ini assert a pytest-timeout Timeout in the nested run (RED-first: config arm failed against the old ini before the removal); (3) slow-fixture remedy proven — test_a_marker_covers_legitimately_slow_fixture_time shows a plain @pytest.mark.timeout(N) absorbs fixture time past a tighter ini budget; (4) pyproject ini comment cites 797b-bbc4-01cf-42d5 and 89d5-61da-b621-47f8. Local gates were green pre-push (make lint incl. complexity ratchet, make typecheck, 34 targeted tests) and the Verified run confirms the full suite passes with fixture time charged to tests — no slow-fixture test tripped the 300 s budget. Closing as regression caused-by bold-abeyant-indri (73b8-2d79-3046-44ce), whose commit 6a5c88027c5 introduced timeout_func_only=true and thereby removed the fixture-phase coverage the 89d5 guard had established."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787452404460588001,"uuid":"5fe298db-6bcb-436a-b68e-8f01d9c8fe05"}